<h2>LGBTQ+ friendly influencers</h2>
<p>Influencers can choose to show <strong>LGBTQ+ friendly</strong> on their public profile, so you can find someone who understands. It is their own choice, off by default, and they can change it at any time. We never guess anything about anyone.</p>
<h2 id="lgbtq-channels">LGBTQ+ channels</h2>
<p>An <strong>LGBTQ+ channel</strong> is a channel started by a verified LGBTQ+ creator, for verified LGBTQ+ members. It shows an <strong>LGBTQ+ channel</strong> tag on the profile, and it is visible to everyone in Explore, search and Google. Only verified LGBTQ+ members can call, book, join the queue or ask to be notified.</p>
<h2>Who can start one</h2>
<p>You do not need a YouTube or Instagram channel. You verify your WhatsApp number and your Aadhaar with an OTP (DigiLocker if the OTP does not work). If your Aadhaar shows transgender, that is enough for the Aadhaar part. Otherwise you make a private self-declaration and accept the LGBTQ+ channel rules. Then you record a 10-second <strong>video KYC</strong> selfie video reading a short code, and our team compares your face with your Aadhaar photo. An LGBTQ+ channel always needs video KYC, and you can also connect a YouTube or Instagram channel if you have one.</p>
<p>When you start a channel you also agree that the <strong>LGBTQ+ channel</strong> tag is public on your profile, in search and on Google. That tag is the only thing shown.</p>
<h2>Who can call</h2>
<p>To call an LGBTQ+ channel you complete <strong>video KYC</strong> too: WhatsApp number, Aadhaar, a private self-declaration and a selfie video. Until it is approved, the Call, Book, Join queue and Notify buttons stay locked and show <strong>Verify to call</strong>. You verify once, and it works for every LGBTQ+ channel.</p>
<p>Verified people show a green <strong>Video KYC verified</strong> badge. Verification confirms who someone is. It does not guarantee how anyone will behave.</p>
<h2>Your declaration stays private</h2>
<p>Aadhaar cannot show orientation, so we ask you to declare it yourself. Your declaration is private. It is never shown on your profile, to creators or to other callers. Only a creator's channel tag is public, and only because the creator agreed to it.</p>
<h2>Adults only</h2>
<p>Everyone must be 18 or older.</p>
<h2>Your safety</h2>
<ul><li>Never share your phone number, photos or address.</li><li>Never pay anyone outside the platform.</li><li>Press <strong>#</strong> to end the call and block the caller.</li><li>Threats or demands for money are not allowed. If someone threatens to expose you or asks for money to keep a secret, that is extortion. Do not pay. End the call and report it.</li><li>No human monitors your call. Report anyone who breaks the rules; our team reviews reports before any strike or ban.</li></ul>
<p>See <a href="/safety">the Safety centre</a> for how to report.</p>
<h2>Friendship, not dating</h2>
<p>The same conduct rules apply here as everywhere else. This is a place for friendship and conversation. Sexual talk is not allowed. Read the <a href="/community-guidelines">community guidelines</a>.</p>
<h2>Your data</h2>
<p>An LGBTQ+ channel tag is shown only because the creator turned it on and agreed to it. A caller's declaration is never shown to anyone, and we never sell personal data. Your Aadhaar number and your video are seen only by you and our verification team. Read the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> for details.</p>
